  "id": "DrugBank_DB09345 - MONDO_1405",
  "verbalization": "Pramocaine is implicated in the treatment of Dermatophytosis Of Groin And Perianal Area through a chain of indications involving Sulconazole and Econazole. The evidence suggests that Pramocaine may be used in conjunction with these antifungal agents to manage fungal infections, as both Pramocaine and Econazole are indicated for Tinea Pedis, which is a common cause of Dermatophytosis Of Groin And Perianal Area. The shared indication for Sulconazole and Econazole, which in turn are linked to the target condition, implies a potential mechanism of action involving antifungal activity. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores suggests that the relationship is robust, though the exact mechanism of how Pramocaine contributes to the treatment remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of antifungal agents in the management of fungal infections, with Pramocaine potentially serving as a supportive or adjunctive therapy.",
